{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows","id":872463,"title":"Sidereals, Martial Arts, and Violet Bier of Sorrows","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-23T10:06:37-07:00","id":872463,"title":"Sidereals, Martial Arts, and Violet Bier of Sorrows","content":"<b>MARTIAL ARTS</b><br /> <i>Peerless Masters of the Martial Arts</i><br /> No constellation governs the Martial Arts. All constellations govern the Martial Arts. Enlightenment is found not in Creation, nor Heaven, nor Hell, but by turning within. Strength is controlling others; power is controlling oneself. This is the Essence of Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal Exalted are often considered the peerless masters of martial arts; the motions and emulations of the styles come as naturally to them as their ability to weave fate and destiny. As mentioned in Character Creation (pg. XX), all Sidereals gain the Martial Arts merit for free, and may purchase dots in any Martial Arts ability and any Martial Arts Charms as Favored.<br /> <br /> However, Sidereals do not exhibit the casual mastery that Solars or the recently appeared Abyssals do. While they have a deep relationship with Martial Arts, they lack the raw power needed to automatically make full use of Martial Arts charms.<br /> <br /> <i>Mastery</i><br /> As described in the core book (pg. 427), Sidereals can access the Mastery effects of Martial Arts charms through their own esoteric methods. These methods include:<br /> * When a Sidereal performs the special action action for a Style\u2019s Form Charm, they may use that Style\u2019s charms with the Mastery effect for the remainder of the scene.<br /> * A Sidereal that has mastered a martial art may craft a Master\u2019s Sutra, describing the essence of the Style. By revealing a prayer strip with that sutra and paying 5m, they may use the mastery effects of that style for the remainder of the scene. These sutras are each unique to the Sidereal, as the nature of enlightenment cannot be copied; revealing them reveals the master\u2019s identity.<br /> * When a Sidereal enters a Martial Arts form, they may use that Style\u2019s charms with the Mastery effect as long as they remain in the Form.<br /> <br /> <i>Sidereal Martial Arts</i><br /> <br /> In addition to the traditional forms of Martial Arts practiced in Creation, the Sidereal Exalted practice a collection of secret arts and enlightened techniques, which are collectively known as Sidereal Martial Arts. Until recently, no member of the Exalted Host could learn Sidereal Martial Arts without either being a Sidereal, or being tutored by one- even then, only Solars could match their sifus. It is assumed that Death\u2019s Lawgivers could likewise be trained, but thus far, no Sidereal is known to have taken such a pupil.<br /> <br /> Recently, Rakan Thulio has boasted that the Getiman Exalted outstrip the Chosen of the Maidens in both mastery and enlightenment. That these mysterious Chosen have exhibited secret techniques and enlightened arts comparable to the Sidereals themselves testifies to the impossible truth of this boast. Whether the Getiman Exalted are truly capable of independent mastery of Sidereal Martial Arts, or if they, like the Solars, are simply capable of being taught and have a willing sifu in Rakan Thulio is not known- but it is certain that these mysterious Chosen are capable of matching the Sidereal Exalted\u2019s peerless mastery in one form or another.<br /> <br /> <b>The Violet Bier of Sorrows Style</b><br /> An ancient style, with roots dating back to the beginnings of the First Age or before, the Violet Bier of Sorrows Style is often one of the first Styles mastered by young Sidereals. It expresses Saturn\u2019s fundamental truth to Creation, and can readily serve as an introduction to deeper mysteries.<br /> <u>Violet Bier of Sorrows Weapons:</u> Attacks made with the Violet Bier of Sorrows tend to be heavy, chopping swings and bone-shattering drop-kicks. They can also be used with knives, slashing and chopping swords, staves and seven-section staves.<br /> <u>Armor:</u> Violet Bier of Sorrows Style is incompatible with armor.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><i><b>Secrets of Future Strife</b></i></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 1, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration:</b>: Permanent<br /> <b><b>Prerequisite Charms:</b></b> None<br /> <br /> The only certain truth is death; of all the secrets that Jupiter holds, Saturn knows this one best. By purchasing Secrets of Future Strife, a Sidereal gains a bonus die to all rolls to detect danger and Join Battle. This die counts as one added by a charm.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><i><b>Flight of Mercury</b></i></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b>: Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Secrets of Future Strife<br /> <br /> The only journey that all must walk is that from birth to the grave; of all the journeys that Mercury watches, Saturn knows the destination. Flight of Mercury allows a Sidereal to suddenly explode forward in order to strike at a foe; they advance one range band towards an enemy, and must take either attack or rush. Flight of Mercury can only be used once per scene.<br /> <b>Mastery:</b> If the martial artist crashes the enemy she attacked or rushed when using this charm, she may use it again against another target.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><i><b>Blade of the Battle Maiden</b></i></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b>: Terrestrial, Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b>: One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Secrets of Future Strife<br /> <br /> It is only in death that the struggle ceases; of all the battles that Mars fights, Saturn knows that is one her sister cannot win. Blade of the Battle Maiden enchants the Sidereal\u2019s weapon with this truth. Increase the Overwhelming damage of your attacks by 1 for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <b>Terrestrial:</b> For a Dragon-Blooded to use this Charm, they must make a sacrifice of pain; increase the cost by 1lhl.<br /> <b>Mastery:</b> When the martial artist assumes the Violet Bier of Sorrows Form, they may also reflexively activate Blade of the Battle Maiden by spending an additional 1wp.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><i><b>Joy in Adversity Stance</b></i></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b>: Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Secrets of Future Strife<br /> <br /> It is the temporary and ephemeral nature of love that makes it worth having; of all the joys that Venus knows, Saturn knows they are most keenly felt when lost. Joy in Adversity Stance enhances this understanding; when the martial artist is crashed by an opponent at close range, she may make a reflexive withering attack against him, even if she has already attacked this turn.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Violet Bier of Sorrows Form</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts : The Violet Bier of Sorrows 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Flight of Mercury, Blade of the Battle Maiden, Joy in Adversity Stance<br /> <br /> Meditating on the mysteries of the Gull, the Peacock, the Gauntlet and the Sorcerer, the martial artist embodies the ending of all things and in all things. She gains double 10s on decisive damage rolls. Additionally, her base initiative after resetting from a decisive attack is (Martial Arts) instead of 3.<br /> <b>Special Activation rules</b>: Whenever the martial artist reaches 15+ initative, she may reflexively activate Violet Bier of Sorrows Form.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Death-Parrying Stroke</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m + 2m / success; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts : The Violet Bier of Sorrows 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-only, Terrestrial, Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Violet Bier of Sorrows Form<br /> <br /> At the last moment, the martial artist sees the path of an attack and knocks it aside with a deft twist of essence. Activating the Death-Parrying Stroke costs 2 motes; she may reduce the damage successes rolled on a withering attack made against her by one success per two motes. Death-Parrying Stroke may be used after damage is rolled.<br /> <b>Terrestrial</b>: When a Dragon-blooded uses this Charm, they instead reduce the damage dice rolled on a withering attack made against her by one die per two motes, and must be used before damage is rolled.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><i><b>Life-Severing Blow</b></i></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m / die; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b>: Decisive-only, Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Violet Bier of Sorrows Form<br /> <br /> In the hands of the martial artist is the power of Saturn, to bring an ending to her opponents. Activate Life-Severing Blow when making a decisive attack; if the attack is successful, you may convert up to to Essence damage dice into successes. You must pay for Life-Severing Blow before making your attack.<br /> <b>Mastery:</b> You may convert up to Martial Arts damage dice into successes instead of Essence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><i><b>Metal Storm</b></i></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b>: Decisive-only, Terrestrial<br /> <b>Duration:</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Violet Bier of Sorrows Form<br /> <br /> Come they alone or at the head of a vast host, all eventually yield to Saturn\u2019s blade. The martial artist may make a decisive attack against two separate enemies in close range; she makes one attack roll, and then divides her initiative evenly between them, adding her Essence to the damage of each attack.<br /> <b>Terrestrial:</b> Dragon-blooded do not add their Essence to the damage of the attacks.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><i><b>Conclusion Pursuing Approach</b></i></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b>: Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Death-Parrying Stroke, Life-Severing Blow, Metal Storm<br /> <br /> It is only by both accepting and pursuing the end that one may delay the inevitable conclusion. This knowledge heartens the martial artist, as she stokes her fighting spirit with determination to never give up. When an attack enhanced with Conclusion Pursuing Approach strikes and deals damage, she gains 1 willpower.<br /> <b>Mastery:</b> Enemies dealt damage by Conclusion Pursing Approach also lose 1 willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 04-28-2016, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T16:53:54-07:00","id":872732,"title":"","content":"So a Sidereal can use Mastery as long as they're in the Form, or by using an individual sutra? Just trying to clarify, since I don't think I understand what the third way is.<br /> Why did you decide to make the sutras individual and not style-specific like they presumably used to be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T17:02:29-07:00","id":872734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=872732#post872732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a Sidereal can use Mastery as long as they're in the Form, or by using an individual sutra? Just trying to clarify, since I don't think I understand what the third way is.<br /> Why did you decide to make the sutras individual and not style-specific like they presumably used to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the way it works is like this.<br /> <br /> Uzuki the Silent Blade rolls Join Battle, and gets the highest Initiative score off the bat. This lets her reflexively activate Single Point Form, and since she used the special activation rules, she benefits from the Mastery keyword for her Single Point charms for the rest of the scene, even if she switches to Violet Bier of Sorrows Form.<br /> <br /> Himeko, her Chosen of Serenity Circlemate, instead uses her first action to activate Dreaming Pearl Form manually, rather than use the reflexive activation by disengaging. While in this Form, she gets the benefits of Mastery with her Dreaming Pearl Charms, but <i>only as long as she remains in Dreaming Pearl Form</i>. If she switches to Snake Form, then she loses the Mastery of Dreaming Pearl and instead gains the Mastery benefits of Snake Style charms.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, their friend, Sorrow of Ages Lost activates a Sutra containing his epiphany on the wisdoms of the Silver-Voiced Nightingale, and for the rest of the scene gains the Mastery benefits of that style, even if he never assumes the Nightingale Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T17:04:11-07:00","id":872737,"title":"","content":"Blade of the Battle Maiden seems very pillow fisted, so to speak. And given that it used to be such an awesomely OP charm, I feel like it'd be cool if it was at least impressively good.<br /> <br /> Future Strife, Joy in Adversity and Flight of Mercury are all very solid low essence MA charms, and I like that. But the stance, while the ability is cool and forceful, seems a bit lacking in the sense that I reckon there should be some more effects there. Perhaps, in the manner that it used to damage virtues, the form could allow for the temporary reduction of intimacies? Seems a bit odd but then, you know, Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T17:11:49-07:00","id":872746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=872732#post872732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a Sidereal can use Mastery as long as they're in the Form, or by using an individual sutra? Just trying to clarify, since I don't think I understand what the third way is.<br /> Why did you decide to make the sutras individual and not style-specific like they presumably used to be?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They can use the Mastery effects of a Style if they are in the style's Form. If you have a style that doesn't synergize well, then this'll do ya.<br /> They can use the Mastery effects of a Style for the remainder of the scene, if they have fulfilled the Form's special activation requirement- independently of being in the Form. This gives a way for Sidereals to synergize multiple styles together, without having to have all of them mastered- but requires them to fulfil some esoteric and sometimes downright contradictory requirements. It also gives a way for novices to get Mastery effects before they've gotten to the Form.<br /> They can use the Mastery effects of a Style by activating their Sutra for the Style- flashing a prayer strip and burning some motes. They can only do this after mastering the Style, but it gives them an easy way to synergize across multiple styles, without having to go through the pain of multiple special activations.<br /> <br /> So, three Sidereals; Mike Mercury, Vinny Venus and Justin Jupiter.<br /> Mike knows Kiss of the Sun Concentration from Righteous Devil Style, but that's it.<br /> Vinny knows Snake Style and Tiger Style, both to the Form.<br /> Justin has mastered Snake Style and Tiger Style.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, Anti-Fate Ninjas!<br /> <br /> Mike wants to use Kiss of the Sun Concentration to flamethrower some anti-Fate ninjas. Since he's not a Solar or Abyssal, he doesn't get access to the Mastery effect. If he lands a decisive attack after aiming on the previous turn, however, he becomes able to use the Mastery effect for the remainder of the scene, having fulfilled the special activation requirement.<br /> <br /> Vinny wants to break bad with Tiger and Snake wicked synergies. He considers; if he assumes Snake Form, he can use the Mastery effects for Snake Style. If he assumes Tiger Form, he can use the Mastery effects for Tiger Style. But he really wants both- which he can get by assuming one form and completing the special activation requirements for the other. Snake requires Withering someone above you in initative to being below you; Tiger requires landing a decisive blow which inflicts at least three levels of damage. He decides to enter Tiger Form as a simple action, counting on the Mastery bonuses from Tiger Style to give him full access to Snake before too long.<br /> <br /> Justin also wants to break bad with Tiger and Snake wicked synergies. Luckily for Justin, he's a master of both styles; as a simple action, he enters Snake Form, and reflexively pays 5m to activate his master's sutra of the Tiger Style. He now has access to the mastery effects of both Snake and Tiger Style.<br /> <br /> Make sense?<br /> <br /> Re: Individual Sutras<br /> <br /> Couple of reasons!<br /> First, because the Sutra for Violet Bier of Sorrows is traditionally the Sutra of the Sword, the Scripture of the Expectant Maiden. But I'd eaten that for Integrity.<br /> Second, because on top of not wanting to write a new sutra for VBoS (since I'm not as good at zen koans as Jenna), I *really* didn't want to write new sutras for every other martial arts style.<br /> Third, because of the concept of signature fighting styles being uniquely identifiable by literal calling cards amuses me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T17:13:57-07:00","id":872750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=872734#post872734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the way it works is like this.<br /> <br /> Uzuki the Silent Blade rolls Join Battle, and gets the highest Initiative score off the bat. This lets her reflexively activate Single Point Form, and since she used the special activation rules, she benefits from the Mastery keyword for her Single Point charms for the rest of the scene, even if she switches to Violet Bier of Sorrows Form.<br /> <br /> Himeko, her Chosen of Serenity Circlemate, instead uses her first action to activate Dreaming Pearl Form manually, rather than use the reflexive activation by disengaging. While in this Form, she gets the benefits of Mastery with her Dreaming Pearl Charms, but <i>only as long as she remains in Dreaming Pearl Form</i>. If she switches to Snake Form, then she loses the Mastery of Dreaming Pearl and instead gains the Mastery benefits of Snake Style charms.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, their friend, Sorrow of Ages Lost activates a Sutra containing his epiphany on the wisdoms of the Silver-Voiced Nightingale, and for the rest of the scene gains the Mastery benefits of that style, even if he never assumes the Nightingale Form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly! And with way better names!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T17:17:59-07:00","id":872756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=872750#post872750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Exactly! And with way better names!</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a circle of Sidereals that I use for examples, one of each Caste. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T17:24:03-07:00","id":872758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=872737#post872737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blade of the Battle Maiden seems very pillow fisted, so to speak. And given that it used to be such an awesomely OP charm, I feel like it'd be cool if it was at least impressively good.<br /> <br /> Future Strife, Joy in Adversity and Flight of Mercury are all very solid low essence MA charms, and I like that. But the stance, while the ability is cool and forceful, seems a bit lacking in the sense that I reckon there should be some more effects there. Perhaps, in the manner that it used to damage virtues, the form could allow for the temporary reduction of intimacies? Seems a bit odd but then, you know, Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re: Blade of the Battle Maiden<br /> <br /> I *suspect* you may be underestimating how useful Overwhelming can be, especially against more heavily armored opponents. *Maybe* give it a +1 to damage as well, but I'd be very iffy on that.<br /> <br /> Re: Boosting the Form<br /> <br /> My first pass actually did have it 'numbing' intimacies, preventing them from being used subsequently- but the reason VBoS cut away Virtues before, from a mechanics perspective, was to fuck up spirits that depended on Virtue minimums for Charm usage- something I don't anticipate will have an analog now. It felt like emulating the original for the sake of emulating the original. Then I had it reset to 4 initative instead of 3, and *then* to reducing the penalty for making a failed decisive attack.<br /> <br /> I'm not 100% happy with any of those; I'm *most* happy with 'and your base initiative for reseting becomes 4 instead of 3', but my bowel cognition warns me that thar be monsters in that space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T17:31:07-07:00","id":872764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=872756#post872756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a circle of Sidereals that I use for examples, one of each Caste. ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>... May I steal them, if / when I end up writing intro and chapter fiction for Where Fate Has Led?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T17:51:17-07:00","id":872771,"title":"","content":"This style seems to be very underpowered to me. One dice to initiative (a specialty is cheaper!), open tens to decisive damage (for 5 motes?), one to overwhelming (from not worth the attack to slightly less so)? If terrestrials got charms like these, I would still say they are too damn weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T17:59:02-07:00","id":872773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=872764#post872764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... May I steal them, if / when I end up writing intro and chapter fiction for Where Fate Has Led?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll PM you their profiles.<br /> <br /> Also, the Layout Leak (the second one, the big one) actually had a sample Sidereal that had Blade of the Battle Maiden in their charmset. It was a Supplemental Charm that cost 2m and 1i, instant-duration, with the Withering-Only Keyword. Its effect was lowering the TN for the Withering Damage roll by 1 for that attack.<br /> <br /> This may be subject to change when the Sid book comes out, of course, but it may be worth using.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T05:38:55-07:00","id":873032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=872771#post872771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This style seems to be very underpowered to me. One dice to initiative (a specialty is cheaper!), open tens to decisive damage (for 5 motes?), one to overwhelming (from not worth the attack to slightly less so)? If terrestrials got charms like these, I would still say they are too damn weak.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Secrets of Future Strife isn't in an either-or case; it's a cumulative with any other Join Battle booster.<br /> <br /> Violet Bier of Sorrows Form, I'll confess, is probably under-powered, as is Blade of the Battle Maiden. I'm tinkering with those based on feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T05:40:36-07:00","id":873033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=872773#post872773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll PM you their profiles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Danke!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=872773#post872773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the Layout Leak (the second one, the big one) actually had a sample Sidereal that had Blade of the Battle Maiden in their charmset. It was a Supplemental Charm that cost 2m and 1i, instant-duration, with the Withering-Only Keyword. Its effect was lowering the TN for the Withering Damage roll by 1 for that attack.<br /> <br /> This may be subject to change when the Sid book comes out, of course, but it may be worth using.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeh. I really don't think Martial Arts should get TN reduction- that's very explicitly the Sidereal Schtick (tm), and not something anyone else can do. It's an interesting idea for a Sidereal Charm- but not for Violet Bier of Sorrows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T07:31:28-07:00","id":873077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=872758#post872758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Re: Blade of the Battle Maiden<br /> <br /> I *suspect* you may be underestimating how useful Overwhelming can be, especially against more heavily armored opponents. *Maybe* give it a +1 to damage as well, but I'd be very iffy on that.<br /> <br /> Re: Boosting the Form<br /> <br /> My first pass actually did have it 'numbing' intimacies, preventing them from being used subsequently- but the reason VBoS cut away Virtues before, from a mechanics perspective, was to fuck up spirits that depended on Virtue minimums for Charm usage- something I don't anticipate will have an analog now. It felt like emulating the original for the sake of emulating the original. Then I had it reset to 4 initative instead of 3, and *then* to reducing the penalty for making a failed decisive attack.<br /> <br /> I'm not 100% happy with any of those; I'm *most* happy with 'and your base initiative for reseting becomes 4 instead of 3', but my bowel cognition warns me that thar be monsters in that space.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean<br /> <br /> it's one additional dice in situations where you are already struggling to do anything at all, bringing you up from totally awful to slightly less totally awful in the case of mortal weapons (and I am firmly of the opinion that everything should work with mortal weapons, especially as Sidereal Daiklaves are hardly an assumed thing). For 1 wip if you get the form. A whole simple action and 5m if you don't! Plenty of the time it's an entirely useless benefit, sometimes it's a not very good benefit for a really high cost.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of reducing TNs for damage dice, because that feels very Siddy and it is the signature Sid style. But if we don't like that, then perhaps something like adds your essence to the post soak withering damage pool. Pow! And I'd say that you get it for the scene, and it's the same cost, because then it's a scary powerful charm (but not overly so) and really it should be, as Blade of the Battle Maiden is a bit iconic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","user":"Solar","date":". 04-24-2016, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T08:20:29-07:00","id":873096,"title":"","content":"I agree with Solar on Blade of the Battle Maiden. I am very aware of the benefits of Overwhelming, but I feel it should be a bit more substantial, as it is a fairly expensive Simple Charm. Compare, for example, a single activation of Increasing Strength Exercise, which gives you an arguably far more useful +1 decisive and withering damage for 3m. Moreover, a hypothetical Terrestrial VBoS master would run a mile before sacrificing a precious health level on so weak an effect.<br /> <br /> If I were writing it I would give it +1 Overwhelming and damage to artifact weapons and raise the Overwhelming rate of mundane weapons (including fists) to their artifact equivalent. This makes it both attractive for weapon fighters and for unarmed masters who fight using multiple styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 04-24-2016, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T09:37:10-07:00","id":873137,"title":"","content":"Based on feedback from here and elsewhere...<br /> <br /> CHANGELOG:<br /> * Explicitly added artifact equivalents to Violet Bier of Sorrows Weapons.<br /> * Rewrote Secrets of Future Strife; now imposes a penalty on first target's Defense.<br /> * Significantly increased power of Blade of the Battle Maiden; now increases post-soak damage and ignores hardness.<br /> * Added Terrestrial Willpower cost to Joy in Adversity Stance.<br /> * Increased power of Violet Bier of Sorrows Form by changing base initative on reset after decisive martial arts attack.<br /> * Swapped Conclusion-Pursuing Approach and Life-Severing Stroke positions in the tree.<br /> * Changed Conclusion-Pursuing Approach to trigger on decisive attacks.<br /> * Changed Life-Severing Blow to also drain 1 initative per die converted to a success.<br /> <br /> <b>The Violet Bier of Sorrows Style</b><br /> An ancient style, with roots dating back to the beginnings of the First Age or before, the Violet Bier of Sorrows Style is often one of the first Styles mastered by young Sidereals. It expresses Saturn\u2019s fundamental truth to Creation, and can readily serve as an introduction to deeper mysteries.<br /> <br /> <u>Violet Bier of Sorrows Weapons:</u> Attacks made with the Violet Bier of Sorrows tend to be heavy, chopping swings and bone-shattering drop-kicks. They can also be used with knives, slashing and chopping swords, staves and seven-section staves, as well as their artifact equivalents.<br /> <br /> <u>Armor:</u> Violet Bier of Sorrows Style is incompatible with armor.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Secrets of Future Strife</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 1, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The only certain truth is death; of all the secrets that Jupiter holds, Saturn knows this one best. When the martial artist makes their first attack in the scene, if her target has a lower initiative than she does, reduce his Defense by (higher of Essence or 2).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Flight of Mercury</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Secrets of Future Strife<br /> <br /> The only journey that all must walk is that from birth to the grave; of all the journeys that Mercury watches, Saturn knows the destination. Flight of Mercury allows the martial artist to suddenly explode forward in order to strike at a foe; she advances one range band towards an enemy, and must take either attack or rush action. Flight of Mercury can only be used once per scene.<br /> <b>Mastery</b>: If the martial artist crashes the enemy she attacked or rushed when using this charm, she may use it again against another target.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Blade of the Battle Maiden</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual, Terrestrial, Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Secrets of Future Strife<br /> <br /> It is only when the struggle ceases that there is peace; of all the battles that Mars fights, Saturn knows that is one her sister cannot win. Blade of the Battle Maiden enchants the martial artist\u2019s attacks with this truth. When making a withering attack, she increases her post-soak damage by (higher of Essence or 3). When making a decisive attack, she reduces the target\u2019s Hardness by (higher of Essence or 3).<br /> <b>Terrestrial</b>: For a Dragon-Blooded to use this Charm, they must make a sacrifice of pain; increase the cost by 1lhl.<br /> <b>Mastery</b>: When the martial artist assumes the Violet Bier of Sorrows Form, they may also reflexively activate Blade of the Battle Maiden by spending an additional 1wp.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Joy in Adversity Stance</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-only, Terrestrial<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Secrets of Future Strife<br /> <br /> It is the temporary and ephemeral nature of love that makes it worth having; of all the joys that Venus knows, Saturn knows they are most keenly felt when lost. Joy in Adversity Stance enhances this understanding; when the martial artist is crashed by an opponent at close range, she may make a reflexive withering attack against him, even if she has already attacked this turn.<br /> <b>Terrestrial</b>: Joy in Adversity Stance costs an additional 1wp to activate.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Violet Bier of Sorrows Form</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Flight of Mercury, Blade of the Battle Maiden, Joy in Adversity Stance<br /> <br /> Meditating on the mysteries of the Gull, the Peacock, the Gauntlet and the Sorcerer, the martial artist embodies the ending of all things and in all things. She gains double 10s on decisive damage rolls. Additionally, her base initiative after resetting from a decisive attack is (Martial Arts) instead of 3.<br /> <b>Special Activation rules</b>: Whenever the martial artist makes two consecutive decisive attacks, or makes a decisive attack which kills or incapacitates a non-trivial opponent, she may reflexively activate Violet Bier of Sorrows Form.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Death-Parrying Stroke</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m / success; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-only, Perilous, Terrestrial<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Violet Bier of Sorrows Form<br /> <br /> At the last moment, the martial artist sees the path of an attack and knocks it aside with a deft twist of essence. She may reduce the damage successes rolled on a withering attack made against her by one success per two motes. Death-Parrying Stroke may be used after damage is rolled.<br /> <b>Terrestrial</b>: When a Dragon-blooded uses this Charm, they instead reduce the damage dice rolled on a withering attack made against her by one die per two motes, and must be used before damage is rolled.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Metal Storm</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only, Terrestrial<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Violet Bier of Sorrows Form<br /> <br /> Come they alone or at the head of a vast host, all eventually yield to Saturn\u2019s blade. The martial artist may make a decisive attack against two separate enemies in close range; she makes one attack roll, and then divides her initiative evenly between them, adding her Essence to the damage of each attack.<br /> <b>Terrestrial</b>: Dragon-blooded do not add their Essence to the damage of the attacks.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Conclusion Pursuing Approach</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only, Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Violet Bier of Sorrows Form<br /> <br /> It is only by both accepting and pursuing the end that one may delay the inevitable conclusion. This knowledge heartens the martial artist, as she stokes her fighting spirit with determination to never give up. When a decisive attack enhanced with Conclusion Pursuing Approach deals damage, she gains 1 willpower.<br /> <b>Mastery</b>: Enemies dealt damage by Conclusion Pursing Approach also lose 1 willpower.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Life-Severing Blow</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m / die; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only, Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Death-Parrying Stroke, Metal Storm, Conclusion Pursuing Approach<br /> <br /> In the hands of the martial artist is the power of Saturn, to bring an ending to her opponents. Activate Life-Severing Blow when making a decisive attack; if the attack is successful, she converts up to to Essence damage dice into successes; for each die converted in this way, the target also loses one initiative. She must pay for Life-Severing Blow before making your attack.<br /> <b>Mastery</b>: The martial artist may convert up to Martial Arts damage dice into successes instead of Essence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 04-24-2016, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T10:50:48-07:00","id":873183,"title":"","content":"I have concerns about Flight of Mercury. Am I correct that the Mastery effect allows immediate use of the Charm again upon reset? Because allowing it to continually chain so long as each target in the sequence is Crashed strikes me as something that would get out of hand very quickly. Particularly since it has no Withering-only tag.<br /> <br /> i.e. Use Flight of Mercury -&gt; Crash first target, reap Initiative Break bonus, trigger reset -&gt; Reactivate FoM -&gt; Crash second target, reap Initiative Break bonus, trigger reset -&gt; Reactivate FoM -&gt; Execute the big bad on turn 1 with your giant pile of Initiative -&gt; do victory dance while ST cries into a pool of his own tears.<br /> <br /> Is this intended behavior?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T11:36:28-07:00","id":873193,"title":"","content":"From how I read it, using the Charm doesn't give you the ability to make another attack, you just have to make an Attack or Rush action if you do use it.<br /> <br /> So you could use it, attack someone, then use it again if you crashed them, but unless you can make more attacks you're out of actions.<br /> <br /> Also I like Blade of the Battle Maiden a lot now, but the Form still seems a bit underpowered even with the option to activate BotBM reflexively and the resetting to MA rather than 3. Like, 8m gets you White Reaper form, which does the double 10s and reduced the Drill of Battle Groups and is how you generate Halos that boost your resolve and key off other Charms. I'd say that adding an additional effect that works around intimacies/resolve/etc would be cool. Perhaps successful withering attacks while in the form temporarily reduce a target intimacy level by one to a minimum of minor for the remainder of the scene?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T11:52:47-07:00","id":873206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=873183#post873183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have concerns about Flight of Mercury. Am I correct that the Mastery effect allows immediate use of the Charm again upon reset? Because allowing it to continually chain so long as each target in the sequence is Crashed strikes me as something that would get out of hand very quickly. Particularly since it has no Withering-only tag.<br /> <br /> i.e. Use Flight of Mercury -&gt; Crash first target, reap Initiative Break bonus, trigger reset -&gt; Reactivate FoM -&gt; Crash second target, reap Initiative Break bonus, trigger reset -&gt; Reactivate FoM -&gt; Execute the big bad on turn 1 with your giant pile of Initiative -&gt; do victory dance while ST cries into a pool of his own tears.<br /> <br /> Is this intended behavior?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Flight of Mercury is a Simple Charm, you can't activate it twice in one round.<br /> The Mastery effect just means you can bounce from target to target after crashing them across multiple rounds- without that, you can only FoM to the first target, and then you have to get to any other targets the long ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T12:01:40-07:00","id":873210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=873193#post873193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I like Blade of the Battle Maiden a lot now, but the Form still seems a bit underpowered even with the option to activate BotBM reflexively and the resetting to MA rather than 3. Like, 8m gets you White Reaper form, which does the double 10s and reduced the Drill of Battle Groups and is how you generate Halos that boost your resolve and key off other Charms. I'd say that adding an additional effect that works around intimacies/resolve/etc would be cool. Perhaps successful withering attacks while in the form temporarily reduce a target intimacy level by one to a minimum of minor for the remainder of the scene?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am *profoundly* hesitant to go into 'punching the intimacies out of someone' route. I can't... properly explain why, tho- just bowel cognition that it at best adds complication without increasing strategic depth, and at worst, opens up potential weird or degenerate scenarios. <br /> <br /> Given how few things alter your base initiative (like, I believe it's just Adamantine Fists of Battle right now), I don't think it needs anything else anyways. At this point, I think it would require actual play to illustrate where the balance is at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T12:03:46-07:00","id":873211,"title":"","content":"Also, completely unrelated side note, but this project has been a great excuse for me to better understand Google's scripting tools; I can now write the charms up in a google sheet (which will enable all sorts of neat functions for counting / tracking / comparing / etc) and easily output them formatted for the WW forums, or reddit, or spit them into a Google Doc. So, yay <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T12:46:35-07:00","id":873233,"title":"","content":"Well I've got a Chosen of Endings NPC who needs to fight a Night Caste Ebon Shadow stylist so I can playtest it this coming thursday if you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T13:18:28-07:00","id":873247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=873233#post873233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I've got a Chosen of Endings NPC who needs to fight a Night Caste Ebon Shadow stylist so I can playtest it this coming thursday if you like.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> AWESOMEST!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T17:15:51-07:00","id":877129,"title":"","content":"Sooooooo used this tonight.<br /> <br /> Giving something a fair run is always tricky because fights are defined by circumstance in actual play, and this fight was essentially set up to be bloodless (and it was so). The Sidereal in question was an observer of events, neither Gold or Bronze, here for a few reasons, and the two Solars were both essentially trying to poke their nose into the business of someone they knew was dodgy (but not how or why) and see how they reacted. The Siddie character was originally built on the Single Point style but given both Single Point and Violet Bier can use slashing swords I thought I'd combine them.<br /> <br /> Okay so, the two Solars approached the Sidereals tent. One is a combat focused Night (Ebon Shadow style) the other is an Eclipse with no combat ability to speak of... but powerful sorcery to draw upon. The Siddie thinks that they might kick off, so he activates Blade of the Battle Maiden prior to combat just in case before they notice (I allow both players and NPCs to do this, in order to promote planning and tactical combat). The Solars have a few words with the NPC, and then for various reasons go live. The Night draws a dagger to throw; Join Battle.<br /> <br /> Now, Sidereal Excellencies are pretty incredible. OP as hell, you might say. And the fight ended up pretty one sided, really. The Sid gets the top initiative, reflexively activates Single Point Style. Cool. First use; get some initiative off that Eclipse, which is easily done, and even more easily done because Secrets of Future Strife. Now, the Night is the real threat and is a bit of a distance away so Flight of Mercury closes the distance and then an attack is landed which hits like a fucking avalanche (only a couple of net hits, but BotBM is very useful here). Nearly but not quite crashes the Night. Night goes; withering attack to try and avoid being smashed (think the player panicked a little here but to be fair they were facing an unarmoured enemy and the Night has been very successful with withering smashes to the face. Hit lands well (crap Sid Parry Excellency lol)... but then is really mitigated in effect by Death Parrying Stroke and the double initiative stack of Single Point Style. <br /> <br /> Essentially, at this point, the Sid is clearly dominating and the Eclipse decides that rather than try anything, they should surrender and attempt to negotiate, so he doesn't start casting a spell or anything. The Night agrees and drops her weapons accordingly, with the Sid sitting on a couple of initiative 20 stacks and both of them nearly crashed. Only one turn of combat! Plenty going on, mind. My thoughts;<br /> <br /> Secrets of Future Strife is pretty badass and a nifty little charm that requires no cost and I like that. It doesn't have a massive impact but it does create an aggressive feel to the charm tree that immediately seems to set the stylist up for decisive attacks, the real aim of the style (hard hitting and powerful).<br /> <br /> Blade of the Battle Maiden is really good now but unless you are using the style either screws with your action economy or required planning. I think that's fine, it's a powerful charm with a scene long effect and thus it should have a drawback, the cost is low and therefore the appropriate area to hit it is ease of use. I like this, feels very potent but not requiring a bit of tactical nous. The Maiden of Battle would approve!<br /> <br /> Flight of Mercury is hectic good. WP is quite a cost and only once per scene too, but a relatively easy reset and a great effect which allows you a lot of flexibility. I like this charm a lot. I wonder if wielding a non-form weapon would prevent you from using it? Because it mandates an attack, but not what kind. Perhaps an amendment saying it must be followed by a Rush or an Attack using the Martial Arts ability with a Violet Bier form weapon? Dunno if that's a good MA precedent to set but otherwise I can see this causing queries.<br /> <br /> Death Parrying Stroke is really powerful. Perhaps too powerful? I dunno. Exchanging withering damage for motes seems like a really good economy to me but I can see circumstances where it wouldn't be the case and certainly there's a danger there of overindulging and finding yourself screwed for motes. And I do like that, because I like charms that give you powerful tactical choices but also allow you to screw yourself.<br /> <br /> Didn't get the use the form, sadly, mostly because the activation criteria never came up and the simple action to activate is a bit painful for the small bonus. Being able to activate BotBM at the same time is appealing though. I dunno. I kind of feel like, compared to the other form charms, I'd always rather have them up, especially as the other cool Violet Bier charms don't necessarily need the form at all. The reflexive activation criteria is quite strict and the whole reset to MA doesn't get a lot of use there I'd imagine because you do two decisive, then activate the form, now you need to do withering attacks (which the form doesn't help at all) to set up another decisive and only then do you get the bonus. I think the reflexive activation should, instead, come before using decisive attacks. Perhaps hitting initiative 15+ through a withering attack lets you reflexively turn it on; then it's like &quot;okay it's killin' time!&quot; and boom you're ready to murder. And I think the reset should be MA+3 rather than MA or 3, because that tops out at +2 ini, not that cool.<br /> <br /> Anyway yeah was fun to use, sync'd well with Shining Point, a bunch of low level charms with lots of use and I liked that, feels very much like the kind of MA that you'd learn as your first MA (numerous and varied low essence benefits that cover quite a few parts of the combat system) combined with also feeling like the MA that would come out of the Violet Bier of Sorrows, AKA rather killy at the end of the day. But yeah. Form charm needs to be neatened up I feel, other than that, the base charms are in a good place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T17:42:18-07:00","id":877159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=873032#post873032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Secrets of Future Strife isn't in an either-or case; it's a cumulative with any other Join Battle booster.<br /> <br /> Violet Bier of Sorrows Form, I'll confess, is probably under-powered, as is Blade of the Battle Maiden. I'm tinkering with those based on feedback.</div> </div> </div> </div>About SFS, even taking it as a not either-or, it's still very limited, and worse in all ways than buying a dot on awareness or perception (these add to the cap, the charm subtracts). Even if it was a non-charm die, still underwhelming. Charms should be like precious chocolates, not something almost imperceptible.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, the new version is much better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T17:47:57-07:00","id":877163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=877129#post877129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooooooo used this tonight.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wmzyYquMS2I\" data-code=\"wmzyYquMS2I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wmzyYquMS2I/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=877129#post877129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flight of Mercury is hectic good. WP is quite a cost and only once per scene too, but a relatively easy reset and a great effect which allows you a lot of flexibility. I like this charm a lot. I wonder if wielding a non-form weapon would prevent you from using it? Because it mandates an attack, but not what kind. Perhaps an amendment saying it must be followed by a Rush or an Attack using the Martial Arts ability with a Violet Bier form weapon? Dunno if that's a good MA precedent to set but otherwise I can see this causing queries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm. It feels like it should be a violet biers weapon, but hard codin that seems... inelegant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=877129#post877129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death Parrying Stroke is really powerful. Perhaps too powerful? I dunno. Exchanging withering damage for motes seems like a really good economy to me but I can see circumstances where it wouldn't be the case and certainly there's a danger there of overindulging and finding yourself screwed for motes. And I do like that, because I like charms that give you powerful tactical choices but also allow you to screw yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm. Maybe it needs a flat activation cost of 2m and then 2m / success.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=877129#post877129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't get the use the form, sadly, mostly because the activation criteria never came up and the simple action to activate is a bit painful for the small bonus. Being able to activate BotBM at the same time is appealing though. I dunno. I kind of feel like, compared to the other form charms, I'd always rather have them up, especially as the other cool Violet Bier charms don't necessarily need the form at all. The reflexive activation criteria is quite strict and the whole reset to MA doesn't get a lot of use there I'd imagine because you do two decisive, then activate the form, now you need to do withering attacks (which the form doesn't help at all) to set up another decisive and only then do you get the bonus. I think the reflexive activation should, instead, come before using decisive attacks. Perhaps hitting initiative 15+ through a withering attack lets you reflexively turn it on; then it's like &quot;okay it's killin' time!&quot; and boom you're ready to murder. And I think the reset should be MA+3 rather than MA or 3, because that tops out at +2 ini, not that cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reflexive stance idea is pretty awesome. Gonna use it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That said, I would really be leery of bumping to MA + 3; that would mean someone could continiously and for free throw out 8 damage attacks, which is rapidly veering towards the kind of escalation of lethality that led to perfect or die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/872463-sidereals-martial-arts-and-violet-bier-of-sorrows?p=877129#post877129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway yeah was fun to use, sync'd well with Shining Point, a bunch of low level charms with lots of use and I liked that, feels very much like the kind of MA that you'd learn as your first MA (numerous and varied low essence benefits that cover quite a few parts of the combat system) combined with also feeling like the MA that would come out of the Violet Bier of Sorrows, AKA rather killy at the end of the day. But yeah. Form charm needs to be neatened up I feel, other than that, the base charms are in a good place.</div> </div> </div> </div>How did the players that were on the receiving side feel? Were they frustrated or excited during the fight, even if they were losing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T11:02:56-07:00","id":878872,"title":"","content":"A flat activation cost could be a good idea, but not necessarily. To clarify; I think the charm is powerful but not too powerful. Combat is a mote intensive place to be and spending two motes to reduce enemy successes by one is good but potentially the kind of economy that sees you unable to use your excellencies much sooner than you thought. Glad you like the idea for the reflexive stance! I can see why you might be concerned about the MA+3 Ini, esp with Blade of the Battle Maiden's Hardness reducer. I dunno. The form isn't super great outside of that reflexive activation, is all I am saying, and thus it's like, commit 8m (less painful if you're in a form I know) to activate this other really cool charm reflexively and I guess double 10s on Decisive too, but lose your other form charm (like Single Point! Or Dreaming Pearl! So good!) while you do it. Booo.<br /> <br /> The players were fine. They had a plan, which was stick their neck out, and it worked. They could have died but they didn't think this guy would do anything more than kick off a bit if pushed since if he wanted to kill them, he already could have probably done so. And they were right! But as far as the fight goes, no they were fine with it. They were pretty scared but they knew they were fighting against a higher essence martial artist pretty sharpish and thus thought it was only fair that he be really deadly. Their only real move was to surrender and negotiate, and that worked, so they were actually a bit chuffed with themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}